      "proposition": "The majority will hold that Title IX's prohibition of employment discrimination does not itself authorize employees' private employment-discrimination suits: Sandoval requires distinct congressional intent to provide that remedy, and Title VII's express enforcement scheme weighs against inferring it."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The majority will announce a categorical exclusion of employees' own employment-discrimination claims from Title IX's implied private action, rather than a rule confined to these plaintiffs or public universities, while preserving student discrimination suits and Jackson-type retaliation suits protecting students."
